From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:06:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0036 the overlay stops buying BTC the client already owns
 (5555 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PHASE1_DECISION chose the OVERLAY as the product on 2026-09-08. The engine
kept buying spot on every entry and selling it on every exit, so the book paid
a four-leg round trip and financing for inventory the client already held.
0032 measured the bill on the settlement clock: $27,232 of fees against
$39,411 of funding, -2.99%/yr at 5% financing.

CARRY_EXECUTION_MODE, required, no default (the two modes send different
orders; build_bot refuses without it):

  overlay   short the perp against the client's BTC. One order in, one order
            out. Round trip 11 bps. No borrow. Their spot is never traded.
  acquire   buy the spot leg and sell it again. Round trip 31 bps. As built.

Same corpus, same clock, same impact, same gate constants, 0% borrow:

                      ACQUIRE            OVERLAY
  ungated        +2.24%/yr n=87     +6.99%/yr n=87
  gated          +3.96%/yr n=66     +7.23%/yr n=79

  funding +39,411.36  basis +866.55  fees -9,660.09 (was -27,232.18)
  borrow 0.00 (was -21,490.23)  impact -1,920.43  = NET +28,697.38

The gate admits MORE entries in overlay because it is finally told the truth
about the exit. NO gate constant moved: ASSUMED_HOLD_DAYS, EWMA_ALPHA,
MIN_ENTRY_FUNDING_BPS, NEGATIVE_FUNDING_EXIT_PRINTS are untouched. What
changed is that the round trip stopped being a constant and became an input —
evaluate_entry(round_trip_bps=...) is now REQUIRED.

The venue decides two more things the source used to:

  lot rules   /v5/market/instruments-info. Linear BTCUSDT step 0.001; the
              engine asked for 0.00127 BTC at $79k, which is a REJECTED order
              (INVENTORY F5). Size is snapped down and refused below the
              minimum lot or notional.
  fee rates   /v5/account/fee-rate, this account's own tier, cached per
              process. Unreadable -> FEE_RATES_UNREADABLE and no order: a book
              that cannot price its exit does not open.

Overlay semantics, stated because one of them is a deliberate exception to
"both legs land or neither": nothing the book did not buy can be naked, so a
perp that does not fill leaves the client exactly as they were (no broken
pair, no allowance spent) and a PARTIAL perp fill is a smaller hedged slice,
which is a correct hedge of less inventory. The one thing that can be naked is
shorting MORE than the inventory: the excess is bought back immediately, and
if that fails the book HALTS (OVERSOLD_BEYOND_INVENTORY). Unwinding buys the
perp back and sells none of the client's BTC. The unhedged remainder of their
stack is their exposure, not the book's, and is reported as such.

Registered: carry_overlay_v1@BTCUSDT, measured_in_sample, forward-only holdout
after 2026-09-09T08:00Z. 32 trials, family-wise FPR 80.6%. Still NOT quotable.
Still 62 of 87 trades losing. The median 5.3-day hold still does not pay its
own 11 bps exit — maker execution is the next lever, and a changed exit rule
is a new hypothesis.

Tests first: bot/tests/test_carry_overlay.py, 39 new, plus 9 in
test_carry_backtest.py. No existing assertion changed; fixtures gained the
execution mode, the venue's lot/fee methods, and the explicit acquire round
trip that the deleted default used to supply.

